(   view or an independent copy. If it returns a copy, assigning `['voltage'] = 3.3` modifies that) Tj
T*
(   temporary copy which is immediately discarded, leaving the original `df` completely unmodified!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Best Practice Solution:) Tj
T*
(   Use single-step `.loc` assignment:) Tj
T*
(   `df.loc[df['ch'] == 1, 'voltage'] = 3.3`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Pandas 2.0+ Copy-on-Write \(CoW\) Paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   Under CoW \(`pd.options.mode.copy_on_write = True`\), any DataFrame slice created is guaranteed) Tj
T*
(   to be a shallow view until a write is attempted. When a write occurs, Pandas lazily allocates a) Tj
T*
(   copy of that specific column only, completely eradicating ambiguity and eliminating) Tj
T*
(   `SettingWithCopyWarning`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
