(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain data aggregation and transformation using `groupby\(\)`, `agg\(\)`, `transform\(\)`, and `apply\(\)` in Pandas.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Split-Apply-Combine Workflow:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. `groupby\(key\)`: Partitions rows into groups sharing identical keys.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. `agg\(func_list\)` \(Aggregation\):) Tj
T*
(   Reduces each group into a single summary scalar \(e.g. mean, sum, std\):) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   summary = df.groupby\('module_id'\)['temp'].agg\(['mean', 'std', 'max']\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. `transform\(func\)` \(Broadcasted Group Operations\):) Tj
T*
(   Applies a transformation to each group and returns an output of the EXACT same length as the) Tj
T*
(   original DataFrame, aligned with original indices:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   # Calculate group-wise z-score normalization) Tj
T*
(   df['z_score'] = df.groupby\('sensor'\)['reading'].transform\() Tj
T*
(   lambda x: \(x - x.mean\(\)\) / x.std\(\)) Tj
T*
(   \)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. `apply\(custom_func\)`:) Tj
T*
(   Passes each group as an entire sub-DataFrame to a Python function, enabling flexible) Tj
T*
(   multi-column calculations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Demonstrate handling missing telemetry data in Pandas: detection, deletion strategies, and forward/backward/interpolation imputation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Handling Corrupted and Missing Telemetry Samples:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   In real-world data loggers, wireless packet drops produce missing intervals \(`np.nan`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Detection: `df.isna\(\).sum\(\)` reveals missing counts per channel.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Deletion Strategies:) Tj
T*
ET

