(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain merging, joining, and concatenation of DataFrames with relational database semantics \(Inner, Outer, Left, Right\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Relational DataFrame Combination:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. `pd.merge\(left, right, on='key', how='inner|outer|left|right'\)`:) Tj
T*
(   - Inner Join: Retains only keys present in BOTH DataFrames.) Tj
T*
(   - Outer Join: Retains all keys from both; missing matches are filled with NaN.) Tj
T*
(   - Left Join: Retains all rows from left; adds columns from right where keys match.) Tj
T*
(   - Right Join: Retains all rows from right.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. `pd.concat\([df1, df2], axis=0\)`:) Tj
T*
(   Glues DataFrames vertically \(stacking logs sequentially in time\) or horizontally \(axis=1,) Tj
T*
(   joining synchronized sensor streams\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   # Merge sensor readings with calibration lookup table) Tj
