(   [Problem Statement]: Detail time-series analysis in Pandas: DatetimeIndex, frequency strings, shifting, rolling statistics, and resampling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Time-Series Engineering Pipeline:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import pandas as pd) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 1. Parse timestamps and establish DatetimeIndex) Tj
T*
(   df['time'] = pd.to_datetime\(df['time_str']\)) Tj
T*
(   df.set_index\('time', inplace=True\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 2. Resampling \(Downsampling 1 kHz vibration data to 1-second RMS\)) Tj
T*
(   rms_1s = df['accel'].resample\('1s'\).apply\(lambda s: np.sqrt\(np.mean\(s**2\)\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 3. Time Shifting \(Lag analysis for communication delay\)) Tj
T*
(   df['tx_delayed'] = df['tx_signal'].shift\(periods=5\) # 5 sample delay) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 4. Rolling Statistics \(Moving Average Filter\)) Tj
T*
(   df['smooth_power'] = df['power_w'].rolling\(window='100ms'\).mean\(\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
