(   [Problem Statement]: Explain memory optimization strategies in Pandas: categorical data types, numeric downcasting, and PyArrow backends.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Memory Reduction Techniques for High-Throughput Logs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Categorical Casting: String columns with repeated values \(e.g. state names, sensor IDs\)) Tj
T*
(   store an 8-byte pointer per row plus the string object \(~50 bytes\). Converting via `df['state']) Tj
T*
(   = df['state'].astype\('category'\)` replaces strings with 1-byte integer keys \(`int8`\), saving up) Tj
T*
(   to 90% RAM.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Numeric Downcasting: Default integers are `int64` \(8 bytes\) and floats are `float64` \(8) Tj
T*
(   bytes\). For ADC data that fits within 12 bits, downcasting to `int16` \(`pd.to_numeric\(...,) Tj
T*
(   downcast='integer'\)`\) cuts memory consumption by 75%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. PyArrow Backend \(`pd.read_csv\(..., engine='pyarrow', dtype_backend='pyarrow'\)`\):) Tj
T*
(   Stores data in contiguous Arrow buffers, eliminates Python string object wrappers, enables SIMD) Tj
T*
(   processing, and provides native bitmask null handling.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

