(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Matplotlib animation via `FuncAnimation` and the concept of 'Blitting' for high-refresh oscilloscope displays.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Blitting Mechanics for Real-Time Oscilloscope Animation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   In naive animation, calling `plt.draw\(\)` on each frame re-renders all static elements:) Tj
T*
(   background canvas, tick marks, text labels, and gridlines. This wastes CPU cycles and caps) Tj
T*
(   frame rates below 15 FPS.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Blitting Optimization \(`blit=True`\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Initialization: The static background \(axes, ticks, labels\) is drawn once and its pixel) Tj
T*
(   bitmap is cached in a raster buffer.) Tj
T*
(   2. Frame Update: On every frame iteration, only the updated line artist coordinates are) Tj
T*
(   refreshed: `line.set_ydata\(new_y\)`.) Tj
T*
(   3. Raster Blit: The graphics subsystem restores the cached background bitmap and draws only the) Tj
T*
(   dirty pixel bounding box of the line artist onto the screen, routinely achieving 60+ FPS) Tj
T*
(   real-time rendering.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
