(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how to plot antenna radiation patterns on polar coordinates using `matplotlib.pyplot.polar`.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Polar Radiation Pattern Plotting:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import matplotlib.pyplot as plt) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   theta = np.linspace\(0, 2 * np.pi, 360\)) Tj
T*
(   # Cardioid radiation pattern: E\(theta\) = 0.5 * \(1 + cos\(theta\)\)) Tj
T*
(   E_field = 0.5 * \(1 + np.cos\(theta\)\)) Tj
T*
(   gain_dbi = 10 * np.log10\(np.maximum\(E_field**2, 1e-3\)\) # Floor at -30 dB) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   fig, ax = plt.subplots\(figsize=\(7, 7\), subplot_kw={'projection': 'polar'}\)) Tj
T*
(   ax.plot\(theta, gain_dbi, color='crimson', linewidth=2, label='E-Plane Gain'\)) Tj
T*
(   ax.set_theta_zero_location\('N'\) # Set 0 deg to top) Tj
T*
(   ax.set_theta_direction\(-1\) # Clockwise angle increase) Tj
T*
(   ax.set_rticks\([-30, -20, -10, 0]\) # Radial dBi limits) Tj
T*
(   ax.set_rlabel_position\(45\)) Tj
T*
(   ax.set_title\('Antenna Azimuth Radiation Pattern \(dBi\)', va='bottom'\)) Tj
T*
(   ax.legend\(loc='lower right'\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
