12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Demonstrate optimizing Pandas queries on 50-million-row DataFrames using Dask or Polars lazy evaluation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Lazy Execution and Query Optimization \(Polars / Dask\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   When single-node Pandas runs out of memory on tens of millions of rows, Polars or Dask provide) Tj
T*
(   lazy computation graph optimization:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import polars as pl) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Define lazy execution plan without loading data into RAM) Tj
T*
(   lazy_plan = \() Tj
T*
(   pl.scan_csv\('massive_sensor_logs.csv'\)) Tj
T*
(   .filter\(pl.col\('voltage'\) > 3.0\)) Tj
T*
(   .group_by\('device_id'\)) Tj
T*
(   .agg\([pl.col\('temperature'\).mean\(\).alias\('avg_temp'\)]\)) Tj
T*
(   \)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Execute with multi-core parallelism and predicate pushdown) Tj
T*
(   result_df = lazy_plan.collect\(\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Key Benefits: Predicate pushdown filters rows before reading into memory, and projection) Tj
T*
(   pushdown only parses necessary columns, bypassing 80% disk I/O.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
